<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="terceira-caves-research" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
  <wpt lat="38.727775" lon="-27.214652"><name>Algar do Carvão</name><desc>Class A; 120 m long; 90 m deep; elev 603.0 m; Porto Judeu; survey centroid (SIGCAVA); Show cave run by Os Montanheiros, open to the public since the 1966 visitor tunnel; Monumento Natural Regional (Reserva Geológica 1987, MN since 2004); the crater drops ~45 m in a vertical conduit to a scree ramp, then a second drop to a clear lake, ~90 m total; extremely rare white amorphous-silica stalactites and stalagmites; two spider species are known only from here; first descent 1893; ~60,000 visitors in 2019; new CAVE visitor centre under construction since 10-2024. Entrance elevation: ~583 m commonly published, 629 m in the 1994 table, 603 m from GLO-30 at this point</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.64601" lon="-27.10572"><name>Gruta das Agulhas</name><desc>Class A; 250.5 m long; elev 30.3 m; Porto Judeu; entrance (GBIF); aka Galeria da Salga; Coastal lava tube at Ponta dos Coelhos, base of Pico do Refugo; enter only at low tide with calm sea; cliff descent; initially called Galeria da Salga, and the 1994 paper uses G. da Salga. In 2023 the sea broke the lava platform at the only entrance and visits are now "muito problematica" in rough sea; the 2024-01-04 attempt to open the upstream entrance was abandoned (unstable slabs); the land is private</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.76383" lon="-27.25553"><name>Gruta dos Balcões</name><desc>Class A; 2713 m long; elev 393.3 m; Biscoitos; entrance (GBIF); aka Gruta do Bastião; Longest cave on Terceira (2713 m surveyed; 4421 m per GBIF; possibly 4.6+ km); Terreiro da Macela pastures; PR09TER trail passes nearby; also called Gruta do Bastião (1994); Pico Galiarte pahoehoe field; Nunes 2014 main entrance 38.76320 -27.25355, 186 m from this point</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.78051" lon="-27.25156"><name>Gruta da Branca Opala</name><desc>Class A; 99 m long; elev 229.8 m; Biscoitos; entrance (GBIF); aka Gruta do Rabão; Opal/silica formations; three entrances (one skylight, two collapse); floods completely between survey points 8-11 on heavy-rain days; Pico Galiarte pahoehoe field (&lt;6,600 y BP, Nunes 2014) - the older "Pau Velho 1761" attribution is superseded, the 1761 flow contains no caves; Nunes 2014 main entrance 38.77939 -27.25168, 125 m from this point; alt name G. do Rabão</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.774287" lon="-27.258573"><name>Gruta do Caldeira</name><desc>Class A; 148 m long; elev 297.3 m; Biscoitos; survey centroid (SIGCAVA); Pico Galiarte pahoehoe field (&lt;6,600 y BP, Nunes 2014); an older attribution to the 1761 Pau Velho flow is superseded; walk-in tube under pastures ending in an impassable collapse; 1994 grid ref sits 590 m off - prefer this position (the BDJ 2019 coordinates agree)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.78006" lon="-27.25213"><name>Gruta do Chocolate</name><desc>Class A; 108.7 m long; elev 233.4 m; Biscoitos; entrance (GBIF); Entrance is a 40x40 cm hole; best example of lava-tube formations on the island per Montanheiros; discovered 1987; length 108.7 m per SIGCAVA (an earlier record gives 109.7 m); Pico Galiarte pahoehoe field (&lt;6,600 y BP, Nunes 2014); Nunes 2014 main entrance 38.78067 -27.25210, 68 m from this point</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.68298" lon="-27.06898"><name>Gruta da Madre de Deus</name><desc>Class A; 244.8 m long; elev 68.0 m; Porto Martins; entrance (GBIF); Near ruined Ermida da Madre de Deus chapel (~1690); two entrances; 13.5 m internal pit at the NW end (1994 survey point 24); a crawling squeeze between points 12 and 15; the "Lingua de Sogra" slab; Fonte do Bastardo eruption, 2,000-3,000 y BP</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.75121" lon="-27.25433"><name>Gruta da Malha</name><desc>Class A; 450 m long; elev 498.4 m; Biscoitos; entrance (GBIF); Part of Malha-Balcões-Chamusca system; Natura 2000; Nunes 2014 main entrance 38.74966 -27.25374, 180 m from this point; upstream part revisited 01-02-2024</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.737769" lon="-27.267997"><name>Gruta do Natal</name><desc>Class A; 696.6 m long; elev 542.8 m; Biscoitos; survey centroid (SIGCAVA); aka Galeria Negra; Galerias Negras; Gruta do Cavalo; Show cave run by Os Montanheiros, open since 01-06-1999 - the first lava tube opened to the public in the Azores; easy transit, few floor changes, high ceilings; first Christmas Mass inside on 25-12-1969, a tradition since; the CAMões analogue astronaut mission lived inside 22-28 Nov 2023; originally Galeria Negra, renamed Gruta do Cavalo in 1964 after horse bones were found, Gruta do Natal from 1969; Nunes 2014 main entrance 38.73747 -27.26846, 52 m from this point; IPEA places it in Altares (Angra)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.71350" lon="-27.18174"><name>Furna de Santa Maria</name><desc>Class B; 320 m long; elev 441.3 m; Porto Judeu; entrance (GBIF); Cabrito area; the Montanheiros gallery pairs it with Gruta do Camelo as "Gruta de Santa Maria e do Carmelo", but all catalogues keep them separate</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.751408" lon="-27.267293"><name>Galeria da Queimada</name><desc>Class B; 639.9 m long; elev 468.9 m; Biscoitos; survey centroid (SIGCAVA); aka Cafua Velha; 2nd longest; tube runs N-S; ends near 38.75003 and 38.75253 at lon -27.267; alt name Cafua Velha; Pico Gordo flows, ~4,480 y BP (Nunes 2014); an older attribution to the 1761 Pau Velho flow is superseded; Nunes 2014 main entrance 38.75012 -27.26602, 181 m from this survey centroid; IPEA places it in Altares (Angra)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.73946" lon="-27.27155"><name>Gruta do Coelho</name><desc>Class B; 171.5 m long; elev 534.0 m; Biscoitos; entrance (GBIF); Near Lagoa do Negro; main entrance shaped like a rabbit burrow, three possible entrances, labyrinthine with large collapse zones; Pico do Gaspar fissural system (&lt;12,100 y BP); Nunes 2014 main entrance 38.73857 -27.27026, 150 m from this point; IPEA places it in Altares (Angra)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.77014" lon="-27.25670"><name>Gruta dos Principiantes</name><desc>Class B; 486 m long; elev 336.9 m; Biscoitos; entrance (GBIF); aka Gruta do Pau Velho; Gruta dos Carvoeiros; Near Gruta dos Balcões; alt names Gruta do Pau Velho and Gruta dos Carvoeiros; Pico Galiarte pahoehoe field</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.799258" lon="-27.285273"><name>Algar da Canada do Laranjo</name><desc>Class C; 7 m long; 5 m deep; elev 69.7 m; Altares; official point (SIGCAVA); The 2024-01-11 Montanheiros round could not find the entrance</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.757344" lon="-27.357442"><name>Algar do Biscoitinho</name><desc>Class C; 10 m long; 8 m deep; elev 338.5 m; Serreta; official point (SIGCAVA)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.746735" lon="-27.324201"><name>Algar do Canadão</name><desc>Class C; 5 m long; 5 m deep; elev 952.2 m; Serreta; official point (SIGCAVA); Natura 2000</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.755255" lon="-27.240570"><name>Algar do Chambre</name><desc>Class C; 17 m deep; elev 611.8 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA); Rocha do Chambre area</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.739715" lon="-27.255074"><name>Algar do Funil</name><desc>Class C; 20 m long; 22 m deep; elev 529.7 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.694103" lon="-27.139231"><name>Algar do João Caldo Quente</name><desc>Class C; 15 m deep; elev 346.9 m; Vila de São Sebastião; official point (SIGCAVA); Georeferenced and surveyed 18-01-2024</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.757906" lon="-27.239578"><name>Algar do Juncal</name><desc>Class C; 12 m long; 50 m deep; elev 576.3 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.736463" lon="-27.270503"><name>Algar do Negro</name><desc>Class C; 16 m long; 5.5 m deep; elev 556.5 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA); Near Lagoa do Negro; IPEA places it in Altares (Angra); georeferenced and surveyed 01-02-2024</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.749658" lon="-27.253636"><name>Algar do Outeiro da Doninha</name><desc>Class C; elev 517.4 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.755990" lon="-27.210120"><name>Algar do Pico Alto</name><desc>Class C; 25 m deep; elev 798.1 m; Agualva; official point (SIGCAVA)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.723813" lon="-27.212706"><name>Algar do Pico do Funil</name><desc>Class C; 8 m long; 15 m deep; elev 563.0 m; Porto Judeu; official point (SIGCAVA); Twin of Gruta do Pico do Funil; elev ~580 m. Reported by the Montanheiros on 25-01-2024 to have been completely buried by the landowner in 2021 or 2022, together with the adjacent gruta - effectively destroyed or inaccessible</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.730154" lon="-27.270928"><name>Algar do Pico Gaspar I</name><desc>Class C; 8.5 m long; 14 m deep; elev 571.0 m; São Bartolomeu de Regatos; official point (SIGCAVA)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.728354" lon="-27.269886"><name>Algar do Pico Gaspar II</name><desc>Class C; 8 m long; 19 m deep; elev 580.5 m; São Bartolomeu de Regatos; official point (SIGCAVA)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.763723" lon="-27.345756"><name>Algar dos Funis</name><desc>Class C; elev 373.6 m; Serreta; official point (SIGCAVA); IPEA lists 300 m depth and freguesia Raminho; SIGCAVA says Serreta with depth unrecorded - unresolved. Found obstructed in 1992 and dug at on 22 and 29-01-1995; possibly the algar F. Fouque described in 1873, though a separate "Algar do Fouque" was visited in 2024 - relationship unresolved</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.736020" lon="-27.271261"><name>Algar/Gruta do Mistério</name><desc>Class C; 151 m long; 13 m deep; elev 561.2 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA); aka Algar do Mistério; Gruta do Mistério; Entry via a 12 m pit into 151 m of tube; near Lagoa do Negro; elev ~545 m; discovered 24-12-1990, measured 01-01-1991; IPEA places it in Altares (Angra); georeferenced and surveyed 01-02-2024</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.710401" lon="-27.345695"><name>Algar/Gruta do Pico das Dez</name><desc>Class C; 114 m long; 20 m deep; elev 349.9 m; Santa Bárbara; official point (SIGCAVA); Length 114 m per IPEA; 1994 paper says 60 m. Depth is 20 m per Borges 1994 (the value shown here) against 14 m in the SIGCAVA record - nothing in the sources settles it. Entry pit then gallery, vertical gear; topography and georeferencing redone 11-01-2024</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.749343" lon="-27.345123"><name>Cova do Caldeirão</name><desc>Class C; 25 m long; elev 645.8 m; Serreta; official point (SIGCAVA); Serreta, near Pico Negrão; a second Cova do Caldeirão (Angra/Sé) is catalogued separately and has no known location</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.645009" lon="-27.229331"><name>Fenda do Pico Zimbreiro</name><desc>Class C; 100 m deep; elev 146.1 m; Angra (Sé); official point (SIGCAVA); Tectonic fissure on Monte Brasil; ~100 m deep per IPEA; serious vertical terrain. The Montanheiros visited a "Fenda do Monte Brasil" on 2024-02-22 and the log gives no further detail; probably this same fissure, but no source confirms it, so the two records are kept separate</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.708180" lon="-27.178696"><name>Furna d'Água</name><desc>Class C; 560 m long; elev 413.3 m; Porto Judeu; official point (SIGCAVA); aka Furna de Água; Furna d' Água; Water-supply cave on the W edge of the Guilherme Moniz caldera, fed by strong springs in the Pico do Carvão flow (~2,000 y BP); managed access with occasional guided visits (Pedaços de Mar 03-06-2023; Montanheiros photo expedition 13-06-2025); Wikipedia entrance pin 38.70877 -27.17247</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.795134" lon="-27.195991"><name>Furna da Nascente</name><desc>Class C; 88 m long; elev 63.3 m; Agualva; official point (SIGCAVA); Quatro Ribeiras coast; distinct from Furna das Pombas and Furna dos Ninhos despite the near-identical SIGCAVA coordinates, which are cliff-section anchors</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.797971" lon="-27.244434"><name>Furna da Rua Longa</name><desc>Class C; elev 6.7 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA); Mapcarta mislabels this spot as Furna das Pombas</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.715617" lon="-27.317953"><name>Furna das Feiticeiras</name><desc>Class C; elev 605.6 m; Santa Bárbara; official point (SIGCAVA); aka Algar das Feiticeiras; Outeiro do Bogango; elev ~600 m; also called Algar das Feiticeiras; georeferenced, explored and surveyed 11-01-2024</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.795161" lon="-27.195622"><name>Furna das Pombas</name><desc>Class C; 76 m long; elev 43.0 m; Agualva; official point (SIGCAVA); Sea cave on the PR02TER Baías da Agualva trail; one of three distinct marine-erosion caves on this stretch of the Quatro Ribeiras coast (with Furna dos Ninhos and Furna da Nascente) that share almost one SIGCAVA coordinate - the points are cliff-section anchors, not individual entrances</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.712463" lon="-27.183204"><name>Furna do Cabrito</name><desc>Class C; 200 m long; elev 449.2 m; Porto Judeu; official point (SIGCAVA); Cabrito area; spring-bearing cave in the same Pico do Carvão flow as Furna d'Água; visited on guided activities in 2023 and on the 13-06-2025 photo expedition</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.780761" lon="-27.361876"><name>Furna do Poço Negro</name><desc>Class C; 20 m long; elev 0.0 m; Raminho; official point (SIGCAVA)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.795134" lon="-27.195852"><name>Furna dos Ninhos</name><desc>Class C; 19 m long; elev 60.8 m; Agualva; official point (SIGCAVA); Quatro Ribeiras coast; distinct from Furna das Pombas and Furna da Nascente despite the near-identical SIGCAVA coordinates, which are cliff-section anchors</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.678829" lon="-27.092893"><name>Galeria da Ribeira Seca</name><desc>Class C; 60 m long; elev 171.6 m; Vila de São Sebastião; official point (SIGCAVA); Coordinates recorded and interior photographed 04-01-2024</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.653399" lon="-27.229311"><name>Galeria do Fanal</name><desc>Class C; elev 0.0 m; Angra (São Pedro); official point (SIGCAVA)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.705568" lon="-27.145728"><name>Galeria do Felisberto Joaquim</name><desc>Class C; 30.3 m long; elev 370.9 m; Vila de São Sebastião; official point (SIGCAVA); aka Algar do Felisberto Joaquim; Also called Algar do Felisberto Joaquim - an algar in Felisberto Joaquim's pastures in São Sebastião (1991); georeferenced and surveyed 18-01-2024</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.684016" lon="-27.073595"><name>Galeria do Sequeira</name><desc>Class C; 15 m long; elev 87.2 m; Fonte do Bastardo; official point (SIGCAVA)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.632611" lon="-27.149912"><name>Gruta Brisa Azul</name><desc>Class C; 80 m long; elev 34.4 m; Feteira; official point (SIGCAVA); aka Gruta Briza Azul; Gruta dos Ratões; Gruta do Ilhéu das Cabras; Marine cave on the north face of Ilhéu Pequeno (western islet), Ilhéus das Cabras; boat only, ~10 min from Angra marina; opening about 4 m high at low tide. "Gruta dos Ratões" is another name for this same cave, not a separate one - four independent sources agree (CM Angra/Angrosfera "Gruta Briza Azul ou Gruta dos Ratões"; PdL 2018 pp. 49-52; Borges 1994 lists a single marine cave at the Ilhéus das Cabras, 80 m; dive.visitazores "north face of the western islet"). A coordinate sometimes given under the Ratões name, 38.63030 -27.14340, sits on the south side of the eastern islet - wrong islet and wrong face. Named 28-08-1971 after the launch "Briza Azul". Length 80 m official (SIGCAVA/IPEA/1994) but Barcelos re-measured ~50 m long x 10 m wide x 7-8 m high in 2018; the entry fissure runs surface to ~15 m and divers reach 24 m. SIGCAVA gives the freguesia as Feteira, PdL 2018 and pt.wikipedia say Porto Judeu (the islets were Feteira only 1911-1913); the SIGCAVA value is used here</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.729568" lon="-27.151334"><name>Gruta da Achada</name><desc>Class C; 169.8 m long; elev 320.4 m; Agualva (Fontinhas area); official point (SIGCAVA); GBIF entrance 38.72977 -27.15186; Fontinhas/Agualva lava flow ("Biscoito das Fontinhas", 1994); georeferenced and surveyed 18-01-2024</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.677819" lon="-27.067427"><name>Gruta da Canada das Vinhas</name><desc>Class C; elev 21.5 m; Praia da Vitória; official point (SIGCAVA); Opened by a JCB in 2016 digging a lamppost foundation; ~30 m of sealed tube, roots through the roof fissures but no microbial mats, which the discoverers put down to the cave being closed; PdL 2016 gives the freguesia as Porto Martins, SIGCAVA says Praia da Vitória</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.800658" lon="-27.283759"><name>Gruta da Canada do Laranjo</name><desc>Class C; 30 m long; elev 37.4 m; Altares; official point (SIGCAVA)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.769531" lon="-27.252567"><name>Gruta da Cascata</name><desc>Class C; 198 m long; elev 359.3 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA); Pico Galiarte pahoehoe field (&lt;6,600 y BP, Nunes 2014); an older attribution to the 1761 Pau Velho flow is superseded; second entrance found 14-08-2014 - a 15 m muddy crawl, impassable in winter flooding; georeferenced and surveyed again 01-02-2024</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.783850" lon="-27.252997"><name>Gruta da Chamusca</name><desc>Class C; 11 m long; elev 146.6 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA); Part of Malha-Balcões-Chamusca system</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.747392" lon="-27.259486"><name>Gruta da Malha Grande</name><desc>Class C; elev 495.5 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA); Distinct from Gruta da Malha; two small holes as entrances, max height 2 m, muddy; limonite columns, secondary deposits, roots and lava stalactites (PdL 2014)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.646524" lon="-27.100941"><name>Gruta da Salga</name><desc>Class C; elev 6.2 m; Vila de São Sebastião; official point (SIGCAVA); Coastal; distinct SIGCAVA entry (the 1994 paper also uses Salga as an alt name for Agulhas); ~25 m, max height 70 cm, no notable formations; long known to the Montanheiros but first explored 09-07-2014</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.721512" lon="-27.266823"><name>Gruta da Santinha</name><desc>Class C; 15 m long; elev 511.1 m; São Bartolomeu de Regatos; official point (SIGCAVA)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.767770" lon="-27.254425"><name>Gruta da Terra Mole</name><desc>Class C; 120 m long; elev 366.2 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA); The separately catalogued "Gruta da Terra Mole II" is the Gruta do Martelo (PdL 2014); Pico Galiarte pahoehoe field; filmed by German TV (Galileo X-Plorer) 28-05-2025</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.652708" lon="-27.150092"><name>Gruta das Mercês I</name><desc>Class C; 69 m long; elev 148.7 m; Feteira; official point (SIGCAVA); Canada das Mercês</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.652185" lon="-27.149964"><name>Gruta das Mercês II</name><desc>Class C; 65 m long; elev 139.8 m; Feteira; official point (SIGCAVA); Two entrances (1994 survey)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.700430" lon="-27.050209"><name>Gruta de Santa Catarina</name><desc>Class C; 28 m long; elev 31.8 m; Cabo da Praia; official point (SIGCAVA); Located 25-10-1992, explored 01-11-1992; georeferenced and surveyed 18-01-2024</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.684917" lon="-27.073435"><name>Gruta de Santo António</name><desc>Class C; 302.1 m long; elev 95.7 m; Fonte do Bastardo; official point (SIGCAVA); aka Gruta do Recanto; GBIF entrance 38.68478 -27.07359; alt name G. do Recanto; Fonte do Bastardo eruption, 2,000-3,000 y BP; the 1994 paper gives the freguesia as Porto Martins, IPEA and SIGCAVA say Fonte do Bastardo; georeferenced and surveyed 18-01-2024</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.644971" lon="-27.104628"><name>Gruta do Alicerce</name><desc>Class C; 20 m long; elev 18.0 m; Porto Judeu; official point (SIGCAVA)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.682022" lon="-27.077019"><name>Gruta do Baldio</name><desc>Class C; elev 93.6 m; Vila de São Sebastião; official point (SIGCAVA); aka Gruta dos Baldios; Two entrances, the wider one walled inside against animals, the second much smaller and difficult; ~100 m in two sections split by a collapse, max height 1.5 m, floor and roof original; Pico da Fonte do Bastardo flow; PdL 2014 notes it belongs to Vila de São Sebastião though many place it in Porto Martins</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.735786" lon="-27.151140"><name>Gruta do Biscoito</name><desc>Class C; elev 298.9 m; Agualva; official point (SIGCAVA); Low-ceilinged tube with several openings near the Terceira golf club, named on discovery (PdL 2016); Fontinhas/Agualva lava flow</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.713465" lon="-27.182011"><name>Gruta do Camelo</name><desc>Class C; 255.9 m long; elev 445.2 m; Porto Judeu; official point (SIGCAVA); aka Gruta do Carmelo; Cabrito area; 1994 grid converts to within 7 m of this point; spelling variant Gruta do Carmelo, and the Montanheiros photo gallery pairs it with Furna de Santa Maria as "Gruta de Santa Maria e do Carmelo" - SIGCAVA, IPEA and 1994 all keep them as two caves ~65 m apart</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.746365" lon="-27.271162"><name>Gruta do Cerro I</name><desc>Class C; 191 m long; elev 486.1 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA); IPEA places the Cerro caves in Altares (Angra)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.748880" lon="-27.271252"><name>Gruta do Cerro II</name><desc>Class C; elev 471.8 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA); IPEA places the Cerro caves in Altares (Angra)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.749194" lon="-27.271644"><name>Gruta do Cerro III</name><desc>Class C; 139 m long; elev 468.4 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA); IPEA places the Cerro caves in Altares (Angra)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.710668" lon="-27.184338"><name>Gruta do Esqueleto</name><desc>Class C; 30 m long; elev 452.2 m; Porto Judeu; official point (SIGCAVA); IPEA lists freguesia as Posto Santo; SIGCAVA says Porto Judeu (Cabrito area)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.731868" lon="-27.156401"><name>Gruta do Golfe</name><desc>Class C; 60 m long; elev 314.8 m; Agualva; official point (SIGCAVA); Fontinhas/Agualva lava flow; georeferenced and surveyed 25-01-2024</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.766529" lon="-27.252959"><name>Gruta do Martelo</name><desc>Class C; elev 379.8 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA); aka Gruta da Terra Mole II; Also named Gruta da Terra Mole II - found 10-07-2014, "Martelo" because a hammer was found near the entrance (PdL 2014); two entrances, max height 0.8 m, rain water enters and the floor is mud and debris; same lava flow as the Pau Velho area caves (Pico Galiarte field)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.772242" lon="-27.257365"><name>Gruta do Morro da Azenha</name><desc>Class C; elev 321.9 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA); aka Gruta dos Morros da Azenha; Tube over 120 m with well-defined flow lines, large lateral balconies and lava rendilhada; very narrow muddy sections limit progress (PdL 2014)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.723588" lon="-27.212671"><name>Gruta do Pico do Funil</name><desc>Class C; 60 m long; elev 559.4 m; Porto Judeu; official point (SIGCAVA); Twin of Algar do Pico do Funil. Reported by the Montanheiros on 25-01-2024 to have been completely buried by the landowner in 2021 or 2022, together with the adjacent algar - effectively destroyed or inaccessible</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.766064" lon="-27.251300"><name>Gruta do Terreiro da Macela</name><desc>Class C; elev 378.2 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA); Position disputed: SIGCAVA puts it here, in Biscoitos beside Gruta dos Balcoes, but its discovery record (PdL 2016 Notas Espeleologicas p. 81) places it "a umas centenas de metros" from Gruta do Biscoito, near the Terceira golf club in Agualva (~38.735 -27.15), about 9 km away. Either SIGCAVA misplaced it or two homonymous sites exist. The SIGCAVA point is shown until a source settles it. Low interior, several openings</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.651394" lon="-27.148710"><name>Gruta do Zé Grande I</name><desc>Class C; 60 m long; elev 132.9 m; Feteira; official point (SIGCAVA); Serretinha; length 60 m per IPEA / 31.6 m per 1994 survey</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.651065" lon="-27.152007"><name>Gruta do Zé Grande II</name><desc>Class C; elev 99.5 m; Feteira; official point (SIGCAVA)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.755976" lon="-27.253417"><name>Gruta dos Buracos</name><desc>Class C; elev 467.0 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA); Limonite stalactites, stalagmites and columns; found 06-12-1992 as a set of "buracos" near Pau Velho; Ar/Ar sample for the Pico Galiarte field was taken here</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.709373" lon="-27.182633"><name>Gruta dos Ratos</name><desc>Class C; 100 m long; elev 445.6 m; Porto Judeu; official point (SIGCAVA); IPEA lists Posto Santo; SIGCAVA says Porto Judeu. The 2024-01-25 search failed to find the entrance under dense vegetation</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.736689" lon="-27.270136"><name>Gruta Pequena</name><desc>Class C; 29 m long; elev 550.7 m; Biscoitos; official point (SIGCAVA); Lagoa do Negro area; IPEA places it in Altares (Angra); georeferenced and surveyed 01-02-2024</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.642824" lon="-27.217155"><name>Tubo I do Monte Brasil</name><desc>Class C; 40 m long; Angra (Sé); official point (SIGCAVA); aka Tubo 1 do Monte Brasil; Submarine lava tube off Monte Brasil - IPEA geomorphology field reads "gruta submarina", and the SIGCAVA point falls in the sea (GLO-30 = 0 m), which is consistent; surveyed 1994 by the cave-divers P. Brunet and C. Thomas with A. Silva</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.642527" lon="-27.217211"><name>Tubo II do Monte Brasil</name><desc>Class C; 87 m long; Angra (Sé); official point (SIGCAVA); aka Tubo 2 do Monte Brasil; Submarine lava tube off Monte Brasil - IPEA geomorphology field reads "gruta submarina", and the SIGCAVA point falls in the sea (GLO-30 = 0 m), which is consistent; surveyed 1994 by the cave-divers P. Brunet and C. Thomas with A. Silva</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.66928" lon="-27.32840"><name>Gruta do Camarão (approx)</name><cmt>Approximate: converted from a 1994 military grid reference, good to roughly 300-800 m. Treat as a search area.</cmt><desc>Class D; 30 m long; Cinco Ribeiras; converted 1994 grid (±300-800 m); Officially class D = location unknown; this is a conversion of the 1994 military grid ref - approximate only, and it falls in the sea, so no elevation is recorded; IPEA describes a tube in a sea-cliff (arriba) at Cinco Ribeiras</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.79820" lon="-27.29250"><name>Algar Adérito de Freitas (approx)</name><cmt>Approximate: an anchor on the volcanic cone the cave is named for, not the entrance. Treat as a search area.</cmt><desc>elev 103.6 m; Altares; area anchor (cone); aka Algar do Pico Matias Simão; Pico Matias Simão, a spatter cone on a radial fissure of Santa Bárbara, coastal Altares, 153 m high; not in SIGCAVA. The position shown is anchored on the cone itself: the 1994 grid reference converts to 38.80179 -27.29105, which falls in the sea (GLO-30 = 0 m) - impossible for a land algar. 1994 gives entrance elevation 150 m. Also called Algar do Pico Matias Simão; the 2024-01-11 Montanheiros round searched for the entrance and could not find it</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.76330" lon="-27.08366"><name>Furna da Bugia (approx)</name><cmt>Approximate: converted from a 1994 military grid reference, good to roughly 300-800 m. Treat as a search area.</cmt><desc>elev 76.5 m; Lajes; converted 1994 grid (±300-800 m); Bugia area; not in SIGCAVA</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.67500" lon="-27.33083"><name>Gruta das Cinco Ribeiras (approx)</name><cmt>Approximate: estimated position, not a fix. Treat as a search area.</cmt><desc>16 m deep; elev 0.0 m; Cinco Ribeiras; approximate; Underwater gallery complex in the zone of Porto das Cinco Ribeiras; the dive begins in the natural pool and the cave is entered directly from the shore (pt.wikipedia: "o acesso e feito directamente pela costa"), a boat is not required; galleries down to about 16 m; weak currents, used for initiation and night dives</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.78154" lon="-27.12740"><name>Gruta das Laranjas (approx)</name><cmt>Approximate: converted from a 1994 military grid reference, good to roughly 300-800 m. Treat as a search area.</cmt><desc>20 m long; elev 25.9 m; Lajes; converted 1994 grid (±300-800 m); Ribeira dos Pães; not in SIGCAVA</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.74800" lon="-27.27100"><name>Gruta do Cerro V (approx)</name><cmt>Approximate: an anchor on the neighbouring cave cluster, not a fix. Treat as a search area.</cmt><desc>elev 475.3 m; Biscoitos; area anchor (cave group); Visited 22-02-2024 together with Cerro I, II and III and one unresolved "Gruta do Cerro (?)", so a Cerro IV may also exist; the position is an anchor on the Cerro cluster, not a fix; IPEA places the Cerro caves in Altares (Angra)</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.63165" lon="-27.14645"><name>Gruta dos Piratas (approx)</name><cmt>Approximate: an anchor on the islet pair - the source does not say which islet. Treat as a search area.</cmt><desc>Feteira; area anchor (islet group); Marine-erosion cave along the vertical fractures of the Ilhéus das Cabras tuffs, named by Prof. F. Cota Rodrigues alongside Gruta Brisa Azul; the source does not say which of the two islets, so the position is an anchor on the islet pair; some of the islet caves are subaquatic. As for Brisa Azul, SIGCAVA-style freguesia Feteira is used while PdL 2018 and pt.wikipedia argue for Porto Judeu</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.63180" lon="-27.14360"><name>Travessia do Ilhéu Grande (sem nome) (approx)</name><cmt>Approximate: an anchor on the islet, not the cave opening. Treat as a search area.</cmt><desc>240 m long; Feteira; area anchor (islet); Unnamed in the source - this label is descriptive, not a documented toponym. A fissure on the north side of Ilhéu Grande lets a diver swim 240 m through the islet and come out inside another cave on the channel side, "não sem alguma dificuldade e risco"; the channel cave admits small boats; episodic yellow water at its mouth from suspended tuff. Position is the Ilhéu Grande anchor, confirmed as the eastern islet by GLO-30 height 138 m against the published 147 m</desc><sym>Cave</sym></wpt>
</gpx>
